      en: "The Kigezi Terraces are an extensive agricultural terrace system in the Kigezi Highlands of Uganda. Built by the Bakiga people, they help control erosion on steep slopes. The terraces cover thousands of kilometers and are used for growing potatoes, beans, and maize. This traditional farming method is a model of sustainable agriculture. The terraced landscape is visually striking and a key feature of the region.",
